{"border":"trbl","align":"center"},"E27":{"border":"trbl"},"I27":{"border":"trbl"},"A28":{"border":"trbl"},"B28":{"border":"trbl"},"C28":{"border":"trbl"},"D28":{"border":"trbl","align":"center"},"E28":{"border":"trbl"},"I28":{"border":"trbl"},"A29":{"border":"trbl"},"B29":{"border":"trbl"},"C29":{"border":"trbl"},"D29":{"border":"trbl","align":"center"},"E29":{"border":"trbl"},"I29":{"border":"trbl"},"A30":{"border":"trbl"},"B30":{"border":"trbl"},"C30":{"border":"trbl"},"D30":{"border":"trbl","align":"center"},"E30":{"border":"trbl"},"I30":{"border":"trbl"},"A31":{"border":"trbl"},"B31":{"border":"trbl"},"C31":{"border":"trbl"},"D31":{"border":"trbl","align":"center"},"E31":{"border":"trbl"},"I31":{"border":"trbl"}}$q$::jsonb;
 questions jsonb := $q$[{"n":1,"marks":1,"text":"Make the heading row A1:I1 Bold, give it Yellow fill colour and Center alignment.","solution":"1. Select **A1:I1** (click A1, hold Shift, click I1).\n2. HOME → **Bold** (Ctrl+B).\n3. HOME → **Fill Color ▾** → Standard Colors → **Yellow**.\n4. HOME → **Center** (Ctrl+E).\n\nChecked: every heading cell A1 to I1 is bold, yellow and centred.","criteria":[{"rule":"cells","range":"A1:I1","props":{"bold":[true],"fillColor":["FFFF00"],"align":["center"]}}]},{"n":2,"marks":2,"text":"In column F (Amount) find Amount = Qty × Rate for every item.","solution":"Start every formula with **=** and click or type the cell names.\n1. Click **F2** and type **=D2*E2** → Enter (20 × 40 = 800).\n2. Click F2 again and **double-click the fill handle** (small square at the bottom-right of the cell) to copy the formula down to **F31**.\n\n(=PRODUCT(D2,E2) also works.)\n\nChecked: every cell F2:F31 has a formula with the right amount.","criteria":[{"column":"F"}]},{"n":3,"marks":2,"text":"In column G (Discount) find the Discount = 10% of the Amount for every item.","solution":"10% means 10 out of 100, so the discount is Amount × 10%.\n1. Click **G2** and type **=F2*10%** (or **=F2*0.1** or **=F2*10/100**) → Enter (800 × 10% = 80).\n2. Double-click the fill handle to fill down to **G31**.\n\nChecked: every cell G2:G31 has a formula with the right discount.","criteria":[{"column":"G"}]},{"n":4,"marks":2,"text":"In column H (Net Amount) find Net Amount = Amount − Discount for every item.","solution":"1. Click **H2** and type **=F2-G2** → Enter (800 − 80 = 720).\n2. Double-click the fill handle to fill down to **H31**.\n\nChecked: every cell H2:H31 has a formula with the right net amount.","criteria":[{"column":"H"}]},{"n":5,"marks":2,"text":"In column I (Remark) using the IF function write \"High\" if the Net Amount is 1000 or more (>=1000), otherwise write \"Low\".","solution":"IF checks a condition: **=IF(condition, value if TRUE, value if FALSE)**. Text goes inside double quotes.\n1. Click **I2** and type **=IF(H2>=1000,\"High\",\"Low\")** → Enter (Rough Note Book, net 720 → Low).\n2. Double-click the fill handle to fill down to **I31**.\n\nComparison signs: **>** greater than, **<** less than, **>=** greater than or equal to, **<=** less than or equal to, **=** equal to.\n\nChecked: every cell I2:I31.","criteria":[{"column":"I"}]},{"n":6,"marks":2,"text":"In cells L2, L3, L4 and L5 find the Total, the Highest, the Lowest and the Average of the Net Amount (H2:H31) using the SUM, MAX, MIN and AVERAGE functions.","solution":"1. **L2**: =SUM(H2:H31) → 37449.\n2. **L3**: =MAX(H2:H31) → 3330.\n3. **L4**: =MIN(H2:H31) → 306.\n4. **L5**: =AVERAGE(H2:H31) → 1248.3.\n\nTip: type the formula and select the range H2:H31 with the mouse, or click H2 and press **Ctrl+Shift+↓** to select down to the last row.\n\nChecked: L2, L3, L4 and L5, all with formulas.","criteria":[{"rule":"value","cell":"L2","equals":37449,"formula":true},{"rule":"value","cell":"L3","equals":3330,"formula":true},{"rule":"value","cell":"L4","equals":306,"formula":true},{"rule":"value","cell":"L5","equals":1248.3,"formula":true}]},{"n":7,"marks":2,"text":"In cell L6 count the number of items using COUNTA on Item Name (B2:B31), and in cell L7 count the Books (Category = \"Books\") using COUNTIF.","solution":"**COUNTA** counts every cell that is not empty. **=COUNTIF(range, criteria)** counts the cells that meet one condition.\n1. **L6**: =COUNTA(B2:B31) → 30.\n2. **L7**: =COUNTIF(C2:C31,\"Books\") → 10.\n\nChecked: L6 and L7, both with formulas.","criteria":[{"rule":"value","cell":"L6","equals":30,"formula":true},{"rule":"value","cell":"L7","equals":10,"formula":true}]},{"n":8,"marks":2,"text":"In cell L8 find the total Net Amount of the Stationery items using SUMIF (Category = \"Stationery\").","solution":"**=SUMIF(range, criteria, sum_range)** adds only the rows that meet the condition.\n1. Click **L8** and type **=SUMIF(C2:C31,\"Stationery\",H2:H31)** → Enter → 6309.\n\nThe first range (C) is checked for \"Stationery\", the last range (H) is added up.\n\nChecked: L8 with a formula.","criteria":[{"rule":"value","cell":"L8","equals":6309,"formula":true}]},{"n":9,"marks":1,"text":"Format the range F2:H31 (Amount, Discount and Net Amount) as Accounting Number Format with the ₹ symbol and 2 decimal places.","solution":"1. Select **F2:H31** (click F2, then **Ctrl+Shift+→** and **Ctrl+Shift+↓**).\n2. HOME → **Accounting Number Format (₹)**. It shows 2 decimal places: ₹ 800.00.\n\n(Ctrl+1 → Number → **Currency**, Symbol ₹, Decimal places 2 also counts.)\n\nChecked: F2:H31 in Accounting or Currency format with ₹ and 2 decimals.","criteria":[{"rule":"cells","range":"F2:H31","props":{"numberFormat":["Accounting","Currency"],"currency":[null,"₹"],"decimals":[2]}}]},{"n":10,"marks":2,"text":"Apply All Borders to the complete table A1:I31 and Center alignment to the Qty column D2:D31.","solution":"1. Select **A1:I31** (click A1, then **Ctrl+Shift+→** and **Ctrl+Shift+↓**).\n2. HOME → **Borders ▾** → **All Borders**.\n3. Select **D2:D31** and click HOME → **Center** (Ctrl+E).\n\nChecked: every cell A1:I31 has borders on all four sides, and D2:D31 is centred.","criteria":[{"rule":"cells","range":"A1:I31","props":{"border":["trbl"]}},{"rule":"cells","range":"D2:D31","props":{"align":["center"]}}]},{"n":11,"marks":1,"text":"Apply AutoFit Column Width to the columns A to I.","solution":"1. Select the columns **A to I** (click the column letter A, hold Shift, click I).\n2. HOME → **Format ▾** → **AutoFit Column Width**.\n\n(Double-clicking the line between two column letters does the same.)\n\nDo this after the ₹ format, so the numbers fit.\n\nChecked: AutoFit on the columns A to I.","criteria":[{"rule":"sheet","path":"autoFitCols","includesAll":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"]}]},{"n":12,"marks":1,"text":"Freeze the top row of the sheet so the headings stay visible while scrolling.","solution":"1. VIEW → **Freeze Panes ▾** → **Freeze Top Row**.\n\n(Clicking A2 and choosing Freeze Panes does the same.)\n\nChecked: panes frozen below row 1.","criteria":[{"rule":"sheet","path":"freeze","equals":"A2"}]},{"n":13,"marks":2,"text":"Rename the sheet Sheet1 to \"Sales\" and give the sheet tab Red colour.","solution":"1. **Right-click** the sheet tab **Sheet1** (bottom-left) → **Rename**, type **Sales** → Enter. (Double-clicking the tab also works.)\n2. **Right-click** the tab → **Tab Color** → **Red**.\n\nChecked: the sheet name is Sales and the tab colour is red.","criteria":[{"rule":"sheet","path":"name","equals":"Sales"},{"rule":"sheet","path":"tabColor","equals":["FF0000","C00000"]}]},{"n":14,"marks":2,"text":"With Conditional Formatting highlight the Net Amount cells H2:H31 that are Greater Than 1000 with Green Fill with Dark Green Text.","solution":"1. Select **H2:H31** (click H2, then **Ctrl+Shift+↓**).\n2. HOME → **Conditional Formatting ▾** → **Highlight Cells Rules** → **Greater Than...**\n3. Type **1000**, choose **Green Fill with Dark Green Text** → **OK**.\n\nChecked: a Greater Than 1000 rule with the green style on H2:H31.","criteria":[{"rule":"anyOf","criteria":[{"rule":"sheet","path":"conditionalFormats","includes":{"range":"H2:H31","type":"greaterThan","value":1000,"style":"greenDarkGreen"}},{"rule":"sheet","path":"conditionalFormats","includes":{"range":"H2:H31","type":"greaterThan","value":"1000","style":"greenDarkGreen"}},{"rule":"sheet","path":"conditionalFormats","includes":{"range":"H1:H31","type":"greaterThan","value":1000,"style":"greenDarkGreen"}},{"rule":"sheet","path":"conditionalFormats","includes":{"range":"H1:H31","type":"greaterThan","value":"1000","style":"greenDarkGreen"}}]}]},{"n":15,"marks":1,"text":"Apply Filter to the table A1:I31.","solution":"1. Click any cell of the table, for example **A1**.\n2. DATA → **Filter** (or HOME → Sort & Filter ▾ → Filter, or **Ctrl+Shift+L**). Arrow buttons appear in the heading row.\n\nDo this last, after the formula columns are filled, so the filter covers A1:I31.\n\nChecked: a filter on the table.","criteria":[{"rule":"sheet","path":"filter","in":["A1:I31"]}]}]$q$::jsonb;
 cells jsonb; model_cells jsonb; working jsonb; model jsonb;
begin
 if exists (select 1 from public.excel_efficiency_tests where slug = 'efficiency-test-6') then raise notice 'EXCEL EFFICIENCY TEST 6 already exists'; return; end if;

 select fixed || jsonb_object_agg(chr(65 + i) || (r + 2), pg_temp.excel_cell(items->r->i)) into cells
 from generate_series(0, jsonb_array_length(items) - 1) r, generate_series(0, 4) i;
 working := jsonb_build_object('schemaVersion', 1, 'language', 'English', 'rows', 31, 'cols', 20, 'cells', cells);
 perform public.assert_excel_efficiency_working_matter(working);

 select cells || jsonb_object_agg(ref, cell) into model_cells from (
   select t.key || (r + 2) as ref, pg_temp.excel_cell(vals->t.key->r, replace(t.value, '#', (r + 2)::text)) as cell from jsonb_each_text(templates) t, generate_series(0, 29) r
   union all select key, pg_temp.excel_cell(value->1, value->>0) from jsonb_each(summary_formulas)) x;
 select model_cells || jsonb_object_agg(key, (model_cells->key) || value) into model_cells from jsonb_each(patches);
 model := jsonb_build_object('schemaVersion', '3', 'rows', 31, 'cols', 20, 'cells', model_cells, 'merges', '[]'::jsonb,
   'sheet', $q${"name":"Sales","freeze":"A2","tabColor":"FF0000","filter":"A1:I31","filterHidden":{},"autoFitCols":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"conditionalFormats":[{"range":"H2:H31","type":"greaterThan","value":1000,"style":"greenDarkGreen"}]}$q$::jsonb, 'operations', '[]'::jsonb, 'savedAt', '2026-11-09T00:00:00.000Z');
 perform public.assert_excel_efficiency_document_schema(model);

 insert into public.excel_efficiency_tests (slug, title, language, status, created_by, sequence, auto_publish_results)
 values ('efficiency-test-6', 'EFFICIENCY TEST 6', 'English', 'draft', admin_id, 6, true) returning id into t_id;
 insert into public.excel_efficiency_versions (test_id, version_number, title, language, description, instructions_markdown, question_count, maximum_marks,
   duration_options, passing_marks, working_matter_snapshot, created_by, delivery_pdf, delivery_onscreen, student_question_toggle, model_answer_snapshot)
 values (t_id, 1, 'EFFICIENCY TEST 6', 'English', 'Normal level, about 10 minutes: book-shop sales sheet of 30 items -- basic formulas and everyday formatting',
   $q$1. Carefully read the instructions and solve the questions accordingly.
2. All questions are mandatory.
3. The sheet has 30 items (rows 2 to 31). Fill a formula in row 2, then double-click the fill handle to copy it down to row 31.
4. **Maximum marks** and question-wise marks are shown with the questions.
5. This is a normal-level paper: you can finish it in about 10 minutes. Complete each task directly in the spreadsheet using formulas, not by typing the answers.$q$, 15, 25, array[600, 900, 1200], 9, working, admin_id, false, true, true, model) returning id into v_id;
 update public.excel_efficiency_tests set current_version_id = v_id, current_version_number = 1 where id = t_id;

 for item in select value from jsonb_array_elements(questions) loop
  crit := '[]'::jsonb;
  for c in select value from jsonb_array_elements(item->'criteria') loop
   if c ? 'column' then crit := crit || pg_temp.column_checks(vals, c->>'column');
   else crit := crit || jsonb_build_array(c);
   end if;
  end loop;
  insert into public.excel_efficiency_questions (version_id, question_number, instruction, marks, display_order, solution)
  values (v_id, (item->>'n')::int, item->>'text', (item->>'marks')::numeric, (item->>'n')::int, item->>'solution') returning id into q_id;
  insert into public.excel_efficiency_grading_rules (version_id, question_id, exact_target, expected_operation, expected_value, allocated_marks, additional_criteria)
  values (v_id, q_id, 'hand-written', 'rule-criteria', 'null'::jsonb, (item->>'marks')::numeric, crit);
 end loop;
end $mig$;

-- Check: the model answer scores the full marks of every question, the untouched sheet 0.
select q.question_number, q.marks,
  public.excel_efficiency_score_question(v.model_answer_snapshot, v.id, q.id, q.marks) as model,
  public.excel_efficiency_score_question(public.excel_efficiency_initial_editor_document(v.working_matter_snapshot), v.id, q.id, q.marks) as untouched
from public.excel_efficiency_tests t join public.excel_efficiency_versions v on v.id = t.current_version_id
join public.excel_efficiency_questions q on q.version_id = v.id where t.slug = 'efficiency-test-6' order by q.question_number;

commit;
